WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.900
Meta's CAPEX surge to $33.9 billion this quarter signals continued AI spending for Canadian TFSA investors. This is Modern Investing Techniques, Episode 208. After the tape, we run a CAPEX to revenue screen, put on a simulated micron weekly hold, and closed Toronto Dominion, then tools, quick hits, and the portfolio record. Quick reminder, everything we discuss here is for education and entertainment. The practice investment of the day uses simulated trades with

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:35.720
no real money. I'm not a licensed financial advisor and this isn't financial advice. Always

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:41.066
do your own research before putting real money to work. Technology and financial stocks

00:00:41.066 --> 00:00:46.986
led the session as the AI infrastructure build out kept pulling in capital. The S&amp;P 500

00:00:46.986 --> 00:00:59.146
closed at 7,757.17, up 0.6%. The NASDAQ composite closed at 26,703, up 1.1% on the day,

00:00:59.146 --> 00:01:07.566
up 14.92% year-to-date, and up 19.35% since the practice portfolio opened on March 16th,

00:01:07.606 --> 00:01:18.586
2026. The TSX composite closed at 36,324.99, up 0.6% while energy lagged on softer oil prices.

00:01:19.166 --> 00:01:24.606
The Bank of Canada rate decision is less than two weeks away, with markets pricing steady policy.

00:01:24.606 --> 00:01:32.506
About 14 days ago, we simulated AVGO on open AI chip news, and it closed down 6.58%.

00:01:32.506 --> 00:01:36.786
A reminder that a strong catalyst can still fade without volume confirmation.

00:01:37.626 --> 00:01:41.186
Earning season continues with several large cap reports do this week.

00:01:41.726 --> 00:01:45.326
That spending surge is not just a headline, it is a screen you can run.

00:01:45.906 --> 00:01:49.686
CapEx jumps at the hyperscalers can lead sector allocation shifts,

00:01:49.686 --> 00:01:54.546
If you track year-over-year capital expenditure, rather than the press release dollar figure.

00:01:55.126 --> 00:02:00.226
One practical implementation is to screen for companies whose CAPEX to revenue ratio has

00:02:00.226 --> 00:02:06.066
risen at least 30% over the prior four quarters, using a brokerage screener or a free platform

00:02:06.066 --> 00:02:07.106
such as FinViz.

00:02:07.486 --> 00:02:12.246
I have no financial relationship with FinViz, Yahoo Finance, or interactive brokers.

00:02:12.926 --> 00:02:17.506
Historically this approach has worked best in the early-to-mid phase of a technology cycle,

00:02:17.506 --> 00:02:21.386
when hardware and data center demand outrun software margins.

00:02:21.786 --> 00:02:26.706
The main risk is that elevated spending can pressure near-term free cash flow and trigger

00:02:26.706 --> 00:02:29.906
multiple compression if revenue growth disappoints.

00:02:30.106 --> 00:02:34.846
Pair the screen with the same day volume check before you size anything and focus on the

00:02:34.846 --> 00:02:39.986
ratio of CAPEX to revenue rather than the absolute dollar amount because a smaller company

00:02:39.986 --> 00:02:44.246
lifting that ratio aggressively can be riding the same infrastructure wave.

00:02:44.246 --> 00:02:50.646
Meta spent $18.8 billion on CAPEX in the same quarter last year, which is how fast

00:02:50.646 --> 00:02:53.526
AI build out costs are scaling for hyperscalers.

00:02:54.066 --> 00:02:59.806
Canadian investors can apply the same ratio screen to TSX listed names with US exposure

00:02:59.806 --> 00:03:06.266
and hold them inside a tax-free savings account, or TFSA, without duplicating US-only positions.

00:03:06.946 --> 00:03:12.046
The same discipline applies when you scan suppliers to those hyperscalers where order visibility

00:03:12.046 --> 00:03:17.026
often shows up one or two quarters after the CAPEX announcement. Investors who

00:03:17.026 --> 00:03:21.066
wait for the revenue confirmation rather than jumping at the CAPEX headline

00:03:21.066 --> 00:03:25.386
alone tend to avoid the multiple compression phase that follows when spending

00:03:25.386 --> 00:03:31.612
outpaces results. Micrond Technology, ticker MU, is this week simulated weekly

00:03:31.612 --> 00:03:37.272
hold shares only on the NASDAQ in tech under a valuation entry ahead of earning

00:03:37.272 --> 00:03:43.772
strategy. This is a simulated trade for learning purposes, $1,000 notional, no real money,

00:03:44.212 --> 00:03:49.512
five sessions from entry at the next open. The Motley Fool notes micron could be worth buying

00:03:49.512 --> 00:03:55.172
before its next earnings report given its record of topping estimates, with the October 27th release

00:03:55.172 --> 00:04:01.552
as the dated check, and risk factors still real. The stock is trading near support after recent sector

00:04:01.552 --> 00:04:06.692
rotation, which is why confidence is medium, the earning surprise history and valuation

00:04:06.692 --> 00:04:10.052
support align, yet that rotation remains a headwind.

00:04:10.632 --> 00:04:14.992
Always cross-check sector rotation signals before sizing earnings driven entries.

00:04:15.572 --> 00:04:20.572
The last simulated hold worked because the catalyst was company-specific, so this one stays

00:04:20.572 --> 00:04:24.152
a single unit instead of trying to recover ground with a larger size.

00:04:24.752 --> 00:04:29.152
Stop loss sits 8% below entry to limit drawdown if rotation continues.

00:04:29.152 --> 00:04:35.652
The target is plus 3% to plus 6% over the 5-session window if the earning setup holds.

00:04:36.092 --> 00:04:40.692
In validation is the next earnings report missing consensus by more than 5%.

00:04:40.692 --> 00:04:45.712
Write that line before the position exists because it names what proves the thesis wrong

00:04:45.712 --> 00:04:47.272
while the money is still hypothetical.

00:04:48.052 --> 00:04:51.192
The volume filter on any rebound is the confirmation step.

00:04:51.472 --> 00:04:52.992
Without it, we do not add size.

00:04:53.552 --> 00:04:56.972
We just let the 5-session clock run and evaluate at the horizon.

00:04:56.972 --> 00:05:03.411
in. Toronto Dominion tickered TD was the last simulated weekly hold, a valuation entry

00:05:03.411 --> 00:05:08.451
on an announced normal course issuer bid that reduces share count while capital ratios

00:05:08.451 --> 00:05:18.051
remain intact. We simulated buying at $165.2 on the Tuesday open and exiting at $169.61

00:05:18.051 --> 00:05:26.651
on the Monday close, a six calendar day window. The position gained 2.78% or $27.81 on a

00:05:26.651 --> 00:05:33.211
$1,000 notional. The NASDAQ rose roughly 1% across the same window, so the trade produced

00:05:33.211 --> 00:05:38.331
modest positive alpha in that hold, even as single-name financial exposure can lag

00:05:38.331 --> 00:05:43.711
broader tech rotation on positive news. The issue or bid was a clean company-specific

00:05:43.711 --> 00:05:49.791
catalyst, and it played out inside the window. Rule, always cross-check sector rotation signals

00:05:49.791 --> 00:05:56.275
before sizing earnings driven entries. Yahoo finances earnings ESP screener filters stock showing

00:05:56.275 --> 00:06:01.695
positive expected surprise prediction, or earnings ESP, combined with a favorable

00:06:01.695 --> 00:06:06.735
Zax rank to highlight names more likely to beat estimates. Canadian investors

00:06:06.735 --> 00:06:11.635
can use the free tier to scan both US and TFX names before earning season peaks,

00:06:12.135 --> 00:06:16.835
export the list into a watch list, and set price alerts with daily updates and no

00:06:16.835 --> 00:06:22.515
subscription, so it sits inside a TFSA workflow without extra platform fees. Tech

00:06:22.515 --> 00:06:28.955
Resources posted a 78.21% earning surprise in its most recent quarter and carries a positive

00:06:28.955 --> 00:06:33.175
ESP of 1.24% ahead of its October 29th report.

00:06:33.695 --> 00:06:38.235
The tool combines the most accurate estimate revision with the consensus to flag setups

00:06:38.235 --> 00:06:41.435
where analysts have grown more bullish just before the release.

00:06:42.535 --> 00:06:47.615
Interactive Broker's option chains show real-time bid-ask spreads and open interest for covered

00:06:47.615 --> 00:06:50.875
call or cash-secured put structures on any listed name.

00:06:50.875 --> 00:06:55.575
Think of a covered call like renting out a parking spot on a property you still own.

00:06:56.035 --> 00:07:01.555
You collect the premium while the shares sit there, and the chain view shows the exact premium per contract,

00:07:01.755 --> 00:07:05.055
so you can calculate return on capital at risk for a given strike.

00:07:05.815 --> 00:07:10.595
Users on the Fixed Commission plan can model that capture before placing a simulated trade,

00:07:11.095 --> 00:07:17.115
toggle weekly versus monthly explorations to see how implied volatility changes with each extra week of runway,

00:07:17.115 --> 00:07:21.655
and pick a window that actually lets an earnings reaction develop instead of a one

00:07:21.655 --> 00:07:23.915
week option that dies before follow through.

00:07:24.828 --> 00:07:27.888
Nike is now the smallest holding in the Dow Jones ETF.

00:07:28.568 --> 00:07:35.128
When investors buy $10,000 of that ETF, they now own just $43 of Nike, which is how cap

00:07:35.128 --> 00:07:40.388
weighting can sideline even a blue chip name, so review any Dow ETF holdings for similar

00:07:40.388 --> 00:07:43.588
concentration drift, and consider an equal weight tilt.

00:07:43.588 --> 00:08:05.440
Max Ketner, HSBC's chief multi-assets strategist, told MarketWatch that investors chasing the AI rally need to understand the goal posts are constantly moving, with valuation multiples and growth expectations shifting rapidly, which is why any AI-themed sleeve should be rebalanced against a fixed valuation screen rather than momentum alone.

00:08:05.440 --> 00:08:11.720
pre-clinical tumor growth control moved Rackovina Therapeutics closer to development candidate selection,

00:08:12.140 --> 00:08:19.080
according to the Financial Post. The TSX Venture Name's KT 5000 AI program is an AI-powered

00:08:19.080 --> 00:08:25.060
cancer therapy delivering potent and selective ATR inhibition with CNS-oriented properties,

00:08:25.500 --> 00:08:31.859
so the live watch is financing or partnership news. At the Clearwater Project, E3 Lithium is

00:08:31.859 --> 00:08:36.859
approaching completion of Phase 2 at its demonstration facility, while permitting an off-take

00:08:36.859 --> 00:08:40.019
work continue in parallel on the path to commercial production.

00:08:40.659 --> 00:08:45.739
The live watch on that TSX Venture Lithium developer is any announced strategic partnership

00:08:45.739 --> 00:08:47.299
that could de-risk the timeline.

00:08:48.244 --> 00:08:54.604
The track record restarted on August 18, 2026 under published rules, fixed five session holds,

00:08:55.224 --> 00:08:59.704
entry at the next open, stopper horizon exits, and no discretionary exits.

00:08:59.704 --> 00:09:04.964
earlier simulated trades remain published as the show's history, but they were exited

00:09:04.964 --> 00:09:09.864
on whatever day the evaluating run happened to price, so they cannot tell you whether this

00:09:09.864 --> 00:09:11.064
method beats the index.

00:09:11.704 --> 00:09:15.964
A listener should be able to take the pick, the date, and the stop, and reproduce every

00:09:15.964 --> 00:09:16.904
number we report.

00:09:17.884 --> 00:09:19.104
Reproduceability is the product.

00:09:19.784 --> 00:09:25.824
Under those rules, the matched window alpha versus the NASDAQ stands at minus 33.1% across

00:09:25.824 --> 00:09:27.604
34 rules based trades.

00:09:27.604 --> 00:09:32.964
markets. Across the full published history there are 85 simulated trades at $1,000 each,

00:09:33.464 --> 00:09:43.284
a 52% win rate, cumulative P&amp;L of minus $31.87, average return per trade of minus 0.04%,

00:09:43.284 --> 00:09:51.564
a best trade of plus 20.11%, and a worst of minus 27.14%. The current cold streak is one

00:09:51.564 --> 00:09:56.504
loss, which is why the next entry stays tightly framed instead of sized up to recover ground.

00:09:56.504 --> 00:09:59.124
A beat last quarter is not a forecast.

00:09:59.664 --> 00:10:04.984
You still need a revision that is moving toward you, and two dates written down before a pre-earnings

00:10:04.984 --> 00:10:06.564
idea earns a place on the pad.

00:10:07.580 --> 00:10:12.320
Open your brokerage screener, set a filter for stocks with positive earnings ESP above

00:10:12.320 --> 00:10:15.200
1% and a Zack's rank of two are better.

00:10:15.760 --> 00:10:18.680
Then note the next two earnings dates for any names that appear.

00:10:19.320 --> 00:10:20.480
That is the whole workflow.

00:10:21.080 --> 00:10:25.540
The screen flags the revision, the calendar stops you from buying a story with no event,

00:10:25.540 --> 00:10:30.140
And the dates are what you actually manage, not a vibe that the name usually beats.

00:10:30.840 --> 00:10:34.340
The misconception is that a long beat streak is itself a buy ticket.

00:10:35.324 --> 00:10:40.624
The fix is the filter plus the two dates, then a written invalidation, then a single simulated

00:10:40.624 --> 00:10:43.604
unit, which is the same habit we just put on micron.

00:10:44.284 --> 00:10:49.804
Before we wrap, Micron's consensus revision into the October 27th print is the dated check

00:10:49.804 --> 00:10:54.024
on this week's simulated hold, and the next open is the first volume test.

